211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( Integrated Watershed Management Programme \(IWMP\) is implemented by Department of Land Resources of Ministry of Rural Development, Government of India. Objectives of watershed development projects are to improve productive potential of rainfed / degraded land through integrated watershed management; to strengthen community based local institutions for promotion of livelihoods & watershed sustainability, and to improve the efficiency of watershed projects through cross learning and incentive mechanism.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( Coodu Trust, as a coordinating agency had conducted training and exposure visit at KVK ,Gandhigram,TNAU Coimbatore,TNAU ,Killikulam and Horticulture college,Periyakulam to enhance the knowledge in modern agriculture . The participants were from watershed committee, watershed beneficiaries and SHGs members from  Pudukottai,Ramnad,Virudunagar,Perambalur,Dharmapuri,Krishnagiri and tutucorin district The training topic were Roles & Responsibility of watershed committee, soil and water conservation techniques, Skill development training on micro enterprises, Vermi compositing, organic forming, micro irrigation for field crops etc. Totally 3021.farmers were trained and the details of farmers trained are as follows)
